# Orbit local development environment.
#
# Copy to .env and adjust as needed:  cp .env.example .env
# .env is gitignored. This file must never contain real secrets.

NODE_ENV=development
LOG_LEVEL=info

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL
#
# DATABASE_URL is the single source of the database connection. Drizzle config,
# migrations, repositories, integration tests, and seed scripts read this one
# variable and nothing else — there are deliberately no separate
# POSTGRES_HOST/PORT/USER/PASSWORD parts that could drift out of sync with it.
#
# Local development targets a dedicated role and database on the PostgreSQL
# server already installed on this machine; see README > Local database.
# The password is a throwaway local development credential, not a secret.
#
# docker-compose.yml remains available as an optional alternative. It is not
# required for any check. If you use it, point DATABASE_URL at that container.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://orbit_dev:orbit_local_dev@localhost:5432/orbit_dev

# Database used by `pnpm test:db`. It is TRUNCATED between tests, so it must
# never point at a database holding data you care about. The integration
# harness requires this variable, refuses to fall back to DATABASE_URL, and
# aborts unless the connected database is literally named `orbit_test`.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://orbit_dev:orbit_local_dev@localhost:5432/orbit_test

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Application ports
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB_PORT=3000
DEMO_PORTAL_PORT=3001
API_PORT=3002
API_HOST=127.0.0.1

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local artifact storage (implemented in Task 5). Gitignored.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTIFACT_STORAGE_DIR=./data/artifacts

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SOP drafting (Phase 2.2)
#
# The model provider used to turn free-form SOP text into a draft SOP Graph.
# Optional: without a key the API still starts and every other route works;
# POST /v1/sop-drafts reports that generation is unavailable.
#
# This is a real credential. Keep it in .env, which is gitignored, and never
# commit it or paste it into a document, an SOP, or an issue.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional override; defaults to claude-sonnet-5.
# ORBIT_LLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model spend limits (Phase 2.8, ADR-029)
#
# Total tokens — input plus output — allowed in each scope. Every scope is
# checked BEFORE a model call is made, and the most restrictive one that would
# be exceeded is the one reported. Spend is summed from the `model_usage`
# ledger, which holds one row per provider call.
#
# At drafting time neither an agent nor a run exists yet, so the scopes map
# onto what is real then:
#   GLOBAL     — every call in this deployment.
#   PER_AGENT  — every call for one SOP document. A document is 1:1 with the
#                agent it will become, so before publication the two are the
#                same thing.
#   PER_RUN    — one Generate request: the initial call plus its one repair.
#
# All three default to the values below when unset. Removing a ceiling is
# spelled "unlimited", deliberately — a blank or a zero is something you type
# by accident. Anything else unparseable stops the API from starting rather
# than falling back, so a mistyped ceiling is never silently ignored.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORBIT_LLM_TOKEN_BUDGET_GLOBAL=5000000
# ORBIT_LLM_TOKEN_BUDGET_PER_AGENT=500000
# ORBIT_LLM_TOKEN_BUDGET_PER_RUN=100000

# Per-model rates for the cost ESTIMATE, in USD per million tokens, as
# `model=input:output` pairs. Nothing fetches a price list — this figure is an
# estimate computed from these numbers and is labelled as one everywhere it is
# shown. Models not listed here or in the built-in defaults are costed at a
# conservative fallback rather than at zero.
# ORBIT_LLM_RATES_USD_PER_MTOK=claude-sonnet-5=3:15,claude-opus-5=15:75
